            <ArticleTitle>Transient bilateral osteoporosis of the hip in pregnancy. A case report and review of the literature.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>138-40</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Osteoporosis of the hip is a rare complication of pregnancy, the diagnosis of which can only be determined by radiologic means. Differentiation between osteonecrosis and osteoporosis remains problematic in some cases. Magnetic resonance imaging was reported as useful for the diagnosis of osteoporosis. Treatment of osteoporosis of the hip in pregnancy should be conservative including physical therapy, restricted weight bearing and analgetic therapy. We report an unusual case of bilateral transient osteoporosis of the hip in pregnancy.</AbstractText>
